    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `riskFlag` as a derived, read-only owner attribute that is `true` when **any** of the three risk signals hold, otherwise `false`, following the codebase's established derivation pattern.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`OwnerDerivations.java`** \u2014 Added a pure `riskFlag(Boolean possibleDuplicate, String email, Boolean capacityWarning)` derivation that ORs the three signals:\n   - possible duplicate \u2192 `possibleDuplicate` flag\n   - email domain disposable-adjacent \u2192 reuses the existing `emailDomainIsDisposable` blocklist check\n   - city over its soft capacity \u2192 `capacityWarning` flag\n   \n   Both persisted `Boolean` flags are treated as `false` when `null` (via `Boolean.TRUE.equals(...)`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient getRiskFlag()` getter that delegates to the derivation, consistent with the other transient derived getters (`getSalutation`, `getContactPreference`, etc.).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `riskFlag` boolean property (`readOnly: true`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct auto-maps it by name into the JSON response.\n\n**Notes on interpretation:** \"disposable-adjacent\" was mapped to the existing disposable-domain blocklist check (`emailDomainIsDisposable`), which is the only email-domain classification defined in the codebase. \"Over its soft capacity\" maps to `capacityWarning` \u2014 the persisted flag set at creation when a city holds 40\u201349 owners (the soft threshold below the hard cap of 50).\n\nThe one existing test (`coreRiskFlagFalseNormally`, asserting `riskFlag` is `false` for a normal structured owner) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
